# PLACEHOLDER — this is not a real SHA256 checksum yet.
#
# Comment-only body, by design: every line in this file starts with `#`,
# so it carries zero non-comment/non-empty lines. That is the same shape
# tests/fixtures/audio/jfk-30s.wav.sha256 used before its real audio was
# committed (M2-06 §3), and the exact thing
# .github/workflows/parity-whisper-real.yml's "Detect audio fixture
# presence" step checks for (`grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)' <sidecar> | grep -q .`
# — present only if that finds a line). A future
# .github/workflows/parity-sbv2-real.yml is expected to gate on this same
# shape for the SBV2 fixture family, per
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-sbv2-v2-design.md §10 "CI workflow" /
# "fixture 管理". This file is intentionally still a placeholder until an
# owner runs the real conversion recipe below.
#
# Role: `checkpoint.bert_en` in reference_dump.manifest.json — the
# English DeBERTa v3 BERT-bridge encoder, upstream
# microsoft/deberta-v3-large (MIT), converted to GGUF via
# `vokra-cli convert --model deberta-v3`.
#
# NOT a valid `sha256sum -c` input (no `<hash>  <path>` line) — feeding
# this file to `sha256sum -c` fails loudly, on purpose (FR-EX-08): a
# placeholder must never be silently accepted as a real checksum.
#
# Owner recipe: tests/fixtures/sbv2/README.md. Once a real
# deberta-v3-large.gguf has been produced (via `vokra-cli convert --model
# deberta-v3`), replace this ENTIRE file with the single-line
# `sha256sum` output:
#
#   sha256sum tests/fixtures/sbv2/deberta-v3-large.gguf > \
#     tests/fixtures/sbv2/deberta-v3-large.gguf.sha256
